      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "In the article is analyzed the spectrum of neurologic disturbances in 107 patients with lumbar intervertebral osteochondrosis that were subjected to the subtotal diskectomy and anterior spondylodesis. The authors describe the dynamics of pre-- and post-operative neurologic status. The significance and value of separate signs, pain syndrome, disturbances of sensitivity and changes of reflexes have been established. The results of the operative treatment of the degenerative spine instability have been evaluated in the clinical conditions."},
